good evening and thank you for joining  me  i'm here to share the latest information  we have  about the new omicron variant and how it  may affect us here in wales  it's been just three weeks since the  first cases of the new variant were  identified in south africa  and since then it has traveled around  the world  it is here in the united kingdom and it  is here in wales at the moment the  number of confirmed cases here is low  but they are growing every day  we have to be prepared for cases to rise  quickly and very steeply  just as they have in other parts of the  uk  we're still learning about this new form  of coronavirus but all the information  we have tells us we are facing a very  serious situation  by the end of the month omicron will  have become the dominant form of the  virus in wales  bringing a new wave of infections and  illness  this could then translate into a large  number of people needing hospital  treatment just at a time when the nhs is  already under significant pressure  this welsh government will do everything  we can to protect people's health  and to keep wales  safe  now over the weekend new evidence  emerged about the effectiveness of our  vaccines against omicron  two doses of the vaccine is simply not  enough to give the level of protection  against infection we all need  the booster dose is vital  we have already increased the speed of  the rollout of our booster program  new clinics have opened and operating  hours have been extended  but urgent efforts are now underway to  accelerate the program even further  so that we can offer all eligible adults  an appointment by the end of this year  if at all possible  but this is a huge undertaking  it will be the priority for our nhs over  the coming weeks and please  make getting a booster your priority too  it is the single most important thing  you can do to protect yourself against  coronavirus and this new variant  i want to thank our vaccination teams  for their hard work hard work